== mini-troff sample.ms: a paper
                A Paper to Try the Macros of ms(6) On

                             Claude Code

                            The IX Project

                               ABSTRACT

               This is the abstract: set in from both sides,
          under its word.  It says in two sentences what the
          paper is for.

     1.  Paragraphs

          A paragraph starts with its first line indented, and is
     long enough here to be put on several lines, so that one
     sees where the others start.† The sentence after the
     footnote's mark is in the same paragraph.

     A paragraph with no indent, with a word in italic, one in
     bold, one typed and a ((parenthesis) done by the third
     argument.

     (1)  An indented paragraph hangs from its tag.

     (2)  The width stays for the next.

          •    One level further right.

          A quotation is set in from both sides, as the
          abstract was, for as long as the paragraph lasts.

     1.1.  A Subsection

     Its number has two parts.

     1.2.  Another

     And the second part counts.

     2.  Displays

     A display keeps its lines:

             one line
                 and another, indented

     A program is in its own font:

       int     main(void)
       {
               return 0;
       }

     What is between a keep's two macros stays on one sheet.

     3.  A Table

     In the middle, in a box, numbers under one another:
              ------------------------------------------
                        Table 1: three columns
              ------------------------------------------
              context switch     39                 fast
              fork             1300.5               slow
              a text              0.25   A cell that is
                                         a text of
                                         several lines
                                         is filled in
                                         its column,
                                         with a word
                                         italic in it.
              ------------------------------------------

     4.  A Picture

     Boxes, an arrow, a curve, a macro:
                           readers
                                        Doc.t
                           words
                                 layout

     A Heading with No Number

     Italic from here on, and roman again.  SMALL words and
     larger ones and normal ones.

     __________________________
     † A footnote, said in the middle of a paragraph and written
     at the sheet's foot.
