                           The Sample Book
                             version 0.1

                             Claude Code



     Contents


     1  A counter
        1.1  The loop
           1.1.1  More of it

     A  Indexes



     Chapter 1  A counter

     This book [1] explains a program of IX, a counter of lines,
     as noweb does [2]1. IX. counts with wc and with count();
     again, again. It costs 100% of $5 — no more — in pages 1–2,
     “quoted”, café, bold, typed, SMALL CAPITALS, a%b{c, and
     n2×xi<=10. Its parts are in Section 1.1 and in Table 1.1, on
     page ?; ?? is nowhere, and is not a command.

     1.1  The loop
     ‹function count 1›=   (more in 3)
     int count(FILE *f) {
             int n = 0;
             ‹count() locals 2›
             while ((c = getc(f)) != EOF)
                     if (c == '\n') n++;     /* 100% of the lines */
             return n;
     }

     The local is declared apart:

     ‹count() locals 2›=   (used in 1)
     int c;

     •  a file is read once

     •  % is not a comment here, and a_b.c is a name

     1.  open

     2.  count

     EOF  the end of the file

     1.1.1  More of it
     ‹function count 1›+=
     int count_all(void) { return count(stdin); }

                     --------------------------
                     File   Lines   What
                     --------------------------
                     wc.c      12   the counter
                         both       a cell
                                    across two
                                    columns
                     --------------------------

